From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:26:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 37/90] render: an effect's visible turns it on and off live

An image effect whose `visible` is bound to a user property (or driven
by a script) is now built even when hidden at load, and every frame the
image checks its effects' visibility: when one changed, the passes that
run are chosen again and the chain is set up for them (which FBO each
pass reads and writes, which pass draws to the scene, the layer's
blending moved to the last pass that runs). Before, an effect hidden at
load was never built, and a visible one never left the chain, so a
property or script toggling it did nothing until a reload. An effect
hidden for good (a literal false) is still not built. A script on an
effect's `visible` runs like a layer property's script (thisLayer = the
image). A passthrough layer draws nothing while none of its effects is
visible, as when none could be. `getEffect()` for layer scripts is not
done (SceneScript, one scene).

Origin: ours
Why: user properties toggling effects did nothing live (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B9: E41, 33 scenes)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
